# spec-mirror/ holds byte-for-byte copies of documents whose originals live in the Shipyard
# data dir, and runcoach-api/tests/test_normative_mirror.py compares the two by bytes (T124).
# The originals are not uniform in line endings (one is CRLF, one mixed), so any normalisation
# on add or conversion on checkout would make every checkout differ from the original by
# platform and fail the gate. `-text` stores and checks out the copies verbatim everywhere.
spec-mirror/** -text

# runcoach-api/tests/data/T162-no-regression-rows.csv is the AC21 release gate's evidence, written by
# `t162-gate` with the csv module's CRLF terminator and compared byte-for-byte against the copy in the
# Shipyard data dir by runcoach-api/tests/test_hrv_no_regression_gate.py (T162). Any line-ending
# normalisation on add or conversion on checkout would make the tree copy differ from the original on
# a non-Windows checkout and fail that gate. `-text` stores and checks it out verbatim everywhere.
runcoach-api/tests/data/T162-no-regression-rows.csv -text
